    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000001</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An information content entity that refers to digital creative works and services, and is utilized to organize the resources of NFDI. The most generic kind of a resource and may be associated with any kind of digital creative work, e.g. datasets, collections, metadata; offered products and services, e.g. data portals, data curation, data digitization.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000001</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">obsolete NFDI resource</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="owl:deprecated"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000001</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000001</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">2024-03-25 - Sasha Bruns: 
This class is useful in nfdicore to provide a unified and structured representation of the diverse range of resources that contribute to the NFDI infrastructure. IMO,  it helps to emphasize the scope of resources that can be contributed to the NFDI compared to all information content entites in IAO.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0000012"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000001</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Resource</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000001</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/118</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000002</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process of a scientific or business endeavor that aims to conclude an investigation or to answer a research question.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000002</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">project</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000002</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Why &quot;project&quot; as an occurrent:
- A project typically has a start and end time.
- It involves a sequence of activities, such as planning, conducting experiments, analyzing data, and publishing results.
- It has temporal parts (e.g., Phase 1, Phase 2, review stages).
So, it aligns well with the occurrent category - more precisely, it can be considered a complex process made up of various subprocesses.

But what about the organization or plan behind it?
- The institution running or participating the project would be a continuant (consortium).
- The project plan might be a generically dependent continuant (a kind of information content entity).
- But the project as executed over time is an occurrent.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000002</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/50</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000004</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An object that represents a single human individual.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000004</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">person</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000004</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">2024-03-24. Sasha Bruns - the class is not mapped to NCBITaxon_9606 (homo sapiens) due to different scope of the ontologies. &quot;Person&quot; in nfdicore represents entities with specific roles, responsibilities, and attributes within an organization, and is not limited to its biological characteristics.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000004</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Harald Sack, Tabea Tietz, Sasha Bruns, Etienne Posthumus</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000005</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A site that refers to geographical locations, such as cities, countries, landmarks, and natural environments.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000005</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">place</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000005</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A spatial region, e.g. country, city or district.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000005</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Hessen, Berlin, Schweiz</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000005</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Issue: https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/75</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000006</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An organisation that consists of multiple independent groups and individuals, who join together to collaborate on a specific goal.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000006</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">consortium</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000006</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A consortium of autonomous organizations collaborating towards a shared goal, operating within the framework of an agreement.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000006</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>NFDI4Culture, NFDI-MatWerk, DataPLANT.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000008</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An independent continuant or information content entity that refers to a manifestation of someone&apos;s creative effort. A creative work refers to a digital intellectual or artistic resource, e.g. a dataset, metadata, a guideline, a software and other materials offering relevant information or instructions within their specific domains.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000008</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">obsolete creative work</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="owl:deprecated"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000008</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000008</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">2024-03-22. Sasha Bruns - Unlike schema:CreativeWork, nfdicore:CreativeWork is specialized to cover digital creative works only. Through the mapping to &quot;schema:CreativeWork and &apos;information content entity&apos;&quot;, we exclude material creative works such as real paintings, architectural objects, and other physical artifacts, which fall outside the scope of nfdicore:CreativeWork.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000008</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>TRANSRAZ Data Model, NFDI4Culture Knowledge Graph, Guide for digital collection management at art museums, NFDI4Culture SPARQL Endpoint, Registry for Tools &amp; Services, RADAR4Culture service, etc.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000008</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/122</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000009</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An information content entity that refers to a structured collection of data, organized typically for a specific goal such as analysis, research, or reference. Dataset is structured information about a resource provided by an organization or a person.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000009</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">dataset</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000009</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">2024-04-10. Sasha Bruns: nfdicore:dataset and ioa:data set are not equivalent, due to their differing conceptualizations of what constitutes a iao:data item, which is a superclass of iao:data set. In the nfdicore ontology, a dataset may not necessarily align perfectly with the definition of a data item, since this definition implies a level of accuracy that may not always apply to datasets in their entirety. While a nfdicore:dataset may contain data items, it doesn&apos;t necessarily qualify as a data item itself under the strict definition provided by ioa:dataset. This differentiation helps us avoid ambiguity and ensures that our modeling aligns with the intended semantics.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000009</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Fotothek Bibliotheca Hertziana Max-Planck-Institut für Kunstgeschichte 320px static derivates research dataset (https://doi.org/10.17617/3.SVH2BT)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0100001"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000011</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:OBI_0000260</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000011</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A realizable entity that represents a structured set of intended actions or steps designed to achieve specific objectives or outcomes.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000011</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">obsolete plan</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="owl:deprecated"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000011</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000012</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">readable IRI label</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000014</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000444</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000014</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process of making information, such as literature, music, and software etc., available to the public for sale or for free.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000014</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">publishing process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0100001"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000015</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0020000</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000015</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>An information content entity that is the outcome of a dubbing process and is used to refer to one instance of entity shared by a group of people to refer to that individual entity.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000015</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">obsolete identifier</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="owl:deprecated"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000015</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000016</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/APOLLO_SV_00000008</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000016</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process that has specified output a software product and that involves the creation of source code.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000016</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">software development</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000017</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A role inherent in an agent that is realized when representing, advocating, or communicating on behalf of an organization or group to convey messages or information.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000017</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">spokesperson role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000018</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An event that focuses on scholarly activities and the exchange of knowledge, typically involving presentations, discussions, or collaborations among researchers, academics, and students, often in the context of conferences, workshops, seminars, symposia, or colloquia, to advance a specific field of study or interdisciplinary research.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000018</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">academic event</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000019</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A role inherent in an organization that is realized when coordinating, managing, or supporting academic activities, programs, or research to promote education and knowledge advancement.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000019</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">academic organization role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000020</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A role inherent in an organization that is realized when promoting, regulating, or supporting industry-specific standards, practices, and collaboration to advance sector development and innovation.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000020</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">industry organization role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000021</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A plan that specifies a sequence of tasks, processes, or operations, often involving multiple agents, tools, or systems, to achieve a specific goal or produce a desired outcome.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000021</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">obsolete workflow</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="owl:deprecated"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000021</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000021</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A workflow defines the logical order and dependencies of steps, the roles or entities responsible for each step, and the inputs and outputs required for and produced by each task. It is a realizable entity that can be enacted or executed within a defined context, such as a business process, computational framework, or organizational procedure.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000021</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/125</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000112"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000022</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A journal article, patent application, laboratory notebook, or a book</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000022</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000310</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000022</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A collection of information content entities intended to be understood together as a whole</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000022</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">document</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000023</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An (nfdi) ontology is a data item that coherently represents all components of an ontology, including its versions, variants, modules and other associated artifacts. It is typically denoted by a name and/or an acronym, which is the term we use to communicate about it.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000023</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ontology</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000024</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An ontology variant represents a self-contained, reusable subset of an ontology that provides a specific functionality while maintaining interoperability with the larger ontology. Typically, an ontology is released in different variants, which makes a variant a release artifact.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000024</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ontology variant</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000112"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000025</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>US Patent 6,449,603</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000025</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000313</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000025</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A document that has been accepted by a patent authority</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000025</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">patent</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000026</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An (nfdi) ontology release version represents a particular release of an ontology.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000026</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">ontology release version</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000027</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A file data item is a data item that represents a file stored on a hard drive. It might also include essential attributes like its name, location, download URL, size, type, and timestamps for creation, modification, and access. It might also capture permissions and ownership details to control how the file can be accessed or modified.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000027</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">file data item</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000029</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A document that conveys information, data, or findings, typically structured in a formal or semi-formal manner, to communicate the results of an analysis, investigation, observation, or activity.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000029</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">report</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000029</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A report is created with the intent of informing specific audiences and may include textual descriptions, visualizations, metrics, or conclusions. It is a realizable entity that is produced and maintained as part of a process or workflow.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000030</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A document that organizes and stores source code files, associated metadata, and version history to facilitate the management, sharing, and collaborative development of software projects. It serves as a structured collection of information that tracks changes, maintains integrity, and supports workflows such as version control, branching, and merging.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000030</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">source code repository</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000030</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The source code repository stands for the CONTENT of the repository, which, e.g., you can copy to your hard drive. This distinguishes it from the website class which e.g. is used to publish the content.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An information content entity that specifies the subject area, domain or academic discipline of an entity. An academic discipline, a research field or domain of an entity, e.g. a domain of a data portal or a field of study of a person.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">academic discipline</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">2024-03-26: SB &amp; JW: Following the OMIT Ontology, the academy discilpine is defined as a subclass of bfo:quality (see e.g. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMIT_0001008)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">2024-12-16: TT &amp; JW: An academic discipline is not a quality, as assumed before, but an ICE. A discipline like philosophy or chemistry consists of structured knowledge, theories, and practices. These are abstract entities that represent and encode information.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q12271</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Architecture, Art History, Musicology, Media Studies, Performing Arts</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000100</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/80</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000101</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process that organizes activities and resources to deliver a specific service, ensuring its efficiency, reliability, and alignment with intended goals.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000101</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">service process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000101</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Issue: https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/75</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000102</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An independent continuant that acts autonomously and is entrusted with the authority to represent, negotiate, or act on behalf of another agent.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000102</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">agent</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000102</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A class that represents entities that are capable of autonomous actions, decision-making, or interaction within a given environment, e.g. persons or organizations.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000102</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Torsten Schrade, Linnaea Söhn, Academy of Sciences and Literature Mainz</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000106</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A place that refers to a densely populated urban area.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000106</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">city</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000106</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A city or a town where the thing is located.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000106</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Berlin, Hannover, Kyiv</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000107</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A material entity that represents a collection of material entities intended to be understood together as a whole.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000107</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">collection</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000107</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A tangible collection of valuables published or curated by an organization or a person.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000107</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A collection of arts displayed at the museum</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000110</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A role inherent in an organization that is realized when the organization is a member of a consortium.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000110</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">consortium member role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000111</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process in which the contact information of an entity is provided.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000111</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">contacting process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0000012"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000111</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Contacting</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000114</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A role inherent in an agent that is realized when the agent is a contact point of a resource or a project.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000114</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">contact point role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000115</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process of contibuting or providing information to an endeavor.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000115</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">contributing process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0000012"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000115</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Contributing</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000118</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A role inherent in an agent that provides input, resources, or effort to support or enhance a project, work, or process.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000118</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">contributor role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000119</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A place that refers to a defined geographical area distinguished by its territorial boundaries, governance structure, and sovereignty.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000119</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">country</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000119</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A country where the thing is located.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000121</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10101412</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000121</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Software that provides large amounts of structured data from repositories and archives to the user. Usually the data can be uploaded, accessed, searched and/or downloaded via a web browser.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000121</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">database software</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000122</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10101412</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000122</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The activity of managing and promoting the use of data from their point of creation to ensure that they are fit for contemporary purpose and available for discovery and reuse. For dynamic datasets this may mean continuous enrichment or updating to keep them fit for purpose. Higher levels of curation will also involve links with annotation and with other published materials</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000122</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">data curation service</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000123</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A website that serves as a centralized platform for accessing, managing, and sharing datasets, information, or resources related to a specific topic, theme, or domain.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000123</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">data portal</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000123</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An online platform that provides access to datasets.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000123</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Bach digital, KultSam, MusiXplora</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000131</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An process that represents an organized happening that unfolds in time.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000131</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">event</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000131</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A class that represents entities that occur or unfold in time, typically characterized by a specific organized happening or occurrence with temporal properties.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000131</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">conferences, celebrations, workshops, meetings, or any other specific incident or happening that has been planned somehow.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000134</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A place that refers to a geographical territory forming part of a country.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000134</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">federal state</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000134</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A federal state where the thing is located.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0000134</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Sachsen, Berlin</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
