    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001204</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actamat.2025.120735</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001204</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A Reference Dataset is a dataset that serves as a benchmark or standardized collection of data used for validation, comparison, and reproducibility in scientific research and engineering applications.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001204</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Reference data of materials
- are documented according to certain standards as well as
- are curated (i.e., generated, maintained, preserved, validated) according to certain standards
- are quantitative data sets (i.e., data + their corresponding metadata)
- have been measured or simulated to a particularly high standard, and
- are generated for a material that has either experienced a well-documented process or is reference material
or its composition and structure has been completely characterized.
Reference data of materials can also be derived data from reference data.
These data are distributed with a license (e.g., GPL).
The here addressed standards for documentation, curation and measurement need to be defined for specific
materials characteristics (e.g., creep tests) in terms of domain standards. These domain standards are the
result of a steered community process.
Standards should integrate as much as possible existing standards (e.g., the individual MatWerk domain
standards should be as much as possible consistent).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001204</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">reference dataset</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001204</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>BAM reference data: results of ASTM E139 -11 creep tests on a reference material of Nimonic 75 nickel-base alloy (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7764161)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001204</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/119</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001205</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A Simulation Dataset is a dataset that contains data generated from computational models, numerical simulations, or digital twin environments to predict material behaviors, properties, and interactions.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001205</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">simulation dataset</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001205</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Examples include DFT simulation datasets, molecular dynamics (MD) trajectory files, and phase-field modeling results.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001205</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/119</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001206</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A Large-Scale Facility is a service product that provides specialized, high-capacity infrastructure for scientific research, engineering, or computational purposes, supporting large-scale experiments, simulations, and data analysis in various domains.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001206</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">large scale facility</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:editorialNote"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001206</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>HBN: Concerning the content of ‘Large-Scale Facility’ datasheet and its related knowledge graph, the ‘Large-Scale Facility’ class and its subclasses were created to define the types of used facilituies and respond to competency questions like: what large-scale facilities support research in field X, which organization provide facility Y, what is the contact point with facility Z, etc.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001206</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>European Synchrotron Radiation Facility (ESRF), the Leibniz Supercomputing Centre (LRZ), CERN&apos;s Large Hadron Collider (LHC)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ontology:NFDI_0010013"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>ontology:NFDI_0001206</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>https://github.com/ISE-FIZKarlsruhe/nfdicore/issues/119</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
