    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Material</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">material</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A Material is a Portion Of Matter that may participate in some Manifacturing Process and whose shape is not relevant for its participation in the Manifacuring Process.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">portion of matter</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A material entity that is not demarcated by any physical discontinuities. At some finer level of granularity it is an object aggregate, at some coarser level of granularity it is a fiat object part,but at this level of granularity it is neither.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">engineered material</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An Engineered Material is a Material that is output of a Manufacturing Process.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">behavioral material property</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A property is a material trait in terms of the kind and magnitude of response to a specific imposed stimulus. Generally, definitions of properties are made independent of material shape and size.

(Callister, W.D., Rethwisch, D.G., Materials Science and Engineering, Wiley, 2014)

We only deal with intensive (system-size independent) materrial properties. Extensive properties that depend on the testpiece/specimen/probe size should be found in the respective testing method modules.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000522</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">application of mechanical load</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000522</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An application of mechanical load is the process of applying force or stress to a material to observe its response or measure its properties.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The subclass trees of &quot;Computing Process&quot; are currently still proposals and serve as a working basis for the discussion round with the simulation/workflow domain experts.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Datenverarbeitung</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Rechenprozess</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">computing process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A process that involves the systematic use of computational methods and tools to perform simulations, analyses, or data transformations to achieve specific scientific or engineering goals.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Ein Prozess, der die systematische Verwendung von rechnerischen Methoden und Werkzeugen umfasst, um Simulationen, Analysen oder Datenumwandlungen durchzuführen, um spezifische wissenschaftliche oder technische Ziele zu erreichen.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Gerät</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">device</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A physical or virtual entity used to perform a specific function or task, often involving measurement, manipulation, or analysis of materials.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Ein physisches oder virtuelles Objekt, das verwendet wird, um eine bestimmte Funktion oder Aufgabe auszuführen, häufig im Zusammenhang mit der Messung, Manipulation oder Analyse von Materialien.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000603</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Rolle eines Gerätes</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000603</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">device role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000603</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Rolle, die ein Geräte inne haben kann.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Herstellungsprozess</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">manufacturing process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A planned process that is driven by the primary intent to transform objects
A manufacturing process is always a transformative process.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Ein geplannter Prozess, der von der primären Absicht angetrieben wird, Objekte zu transformieren. Ein Herstellungsprozess ist immer ein Transformationsprozess.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000848</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">mechanical property</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000848</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A mechanical property is a material property that inheres in a material M when an object O_target that consists of M is stimulated in a process through an interaction with an object O_stimulus and M changes its stress/strain/..(mechanical?) SDCs.

TODO: Check general class axiom and defintion altogether !!!</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000849</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Mechanische Eigenschaften Analyseverfahren</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000849</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">mechanical property analyzing process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000849</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An assay that evaluates the mechanical characteristics of materials, such as strength, hardness, elasticity, and tensile properties, often through tests that measure response to forces and loads.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000849</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Eine Analyse, die die mechanischen Eigenschaften von Materialien bewertet, wie z.B. Festigkeit, Härte, Elastizität und Zugfestigkeit, oft durch Tests, die die Reaktion auf Kräfte und Lasten messen.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000857</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">microstructure</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000857</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The microstructure represents the small-scale structure of a material, including grains, phases, and defects, visible under a microscope.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">ANMERKUNG: Ein Sample ist ein Teil (oder das Ganze) eines Probestücks. Das Probestück wird bei der Herstellung eines industriell verwendeten Produktes gezielt für die Überprüfung des Produkteigenschaften bereitgestellt. CAVE: Diese Anmerkung beschreibt das Objekt, welches die Rolle, die durch diese owl:Class definiert wird, realisiert.
ANMERKUNG: Die exakte Wortwahl der EN 10021 wurde verallgemeinert.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">In certain cases, the sample can be the specimen or the test piece itself.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Mitunter kann der Probenabschnitt (Sample) unmittelbar als Prüfling (Specimen) oder Probe dienen.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">NOTE: A Sample is a part (or the whole) of a Sample product. The Sample product is specifically produced portion of an industrially used and traded product for the purpose of determining the properties/quality of the product. CAVE: This note describes the object, that realizes the role defined by this owl:Class.
NOTE: The wording used in EN 10021 was generalized.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">EN 10021:2006-12 (European standardization committee: CEN/TC 459/SC 12/WG 4)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Probe-Rolle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">sample role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Role of an object, which is a quantity of material taken from a (sample) product, that is sufficient for the purpose of obtaining test pieces.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000919</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Rolle eines Objektes, das eine von einem Probestück/Material entnommene Menge ist, welche (vom Umfang her) geeignet ist Proben (Test Pieces) herzustellen.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000950</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">stimulating process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000950</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The stimulating process is a process describing the application of an external influence, such as force, heat, or radiation, to study material response.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000957</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Struktur Eigenschaften Analyseverfahren</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000957</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">structural property analyzing process</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000957</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An assay that examines the external and internal structure and morphology of materials, including the arrangement of atoms, crystals, grains, and phases, often using techniques like microscopy and diffraction.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000957</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Eine Analyse, die die äußere und innere Struktur und Morphologie von Materialien untersucht, einschließlich der Anordnung von Atomen, Kristallen, Körnern und Phasen, oft unter Verwendung von Techniken wie Mikroskopie und Beugung.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">ANMERKUNG: Ein Test Piece ist ein Teilstück (potenziell alles) eines Specimens, welches die Bedingungen erfüllt, die durch ein anzuwendendes Prüfverfahren gestellt werden. Ein Specimen erfüllt diese Anforderungen im Allgemeinen erst nach weiterer Bearbeitung. CAVE: Diese Anmerkung beschreibt das Objekt, welches die Rolle, die durch diese owl:Class definiert wird, realisiert.
ANMERKUNG: Die exakte Wortwahl der EN 10021 wurde verallgemeinert.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">In certain cases, the test piece can be the sample or the specimen itself.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Mitunter kann der Probenabschnitt (Sample) oder der Prüfling (Specimen) unmittelbar als Probe dienen.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">NOTE: A Test Piece is a piece that is taken from a specimen (potentially the whole specimen), which fulfills the requirements, that are set by the test procedure in which the test piece is about to be used. A specimen fulfills this requierements generally speaking only after further treatment/processing. CAVE: This note describes the object, that realizes the role defined by this owl:Class.
NOTE: The wording used in EN 10021 was generalized.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000119"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">EN 10021:2006-12 (European standardization committee: CEN/TC 459/SC 12/WG 4)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Proben-Rolle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">test piece role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="de">Rolle eines Objekts, welches eine Probe ist, die aus einem Prüfling (Specimen) oder Probenabschnitt (Sample) entnommen wurde; die Probe hat festgelegte Dimensionen, kann maschinell bearbeitet sein, wurde in einen für die Verwendung in einem Prüfverfahren notwendigen Zustand gebracht</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000975</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">role of object which is a part taken from a specimen or sample; the part has specified dimensions, is machined or un-machined, brought to a required condition for submission to a given test</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020004</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">composition specification</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:definition"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020004</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Composition specification is an information content entity that is conretized by  composition of a portion of matter and has memebers fraction specifications of portions of other matters (but not chemical elements) of which the whole portion of matter consists of (has parts).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="skos:example"/>
        <IRI>https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020004</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Nitric acid solution has quality  composition , which concretizes the composition specification .The composition specification has parts fraction specifications of nitric acid, e.g., 4 vol.%, and distilled water. These fraction specifications specify value of pure substances of nitric acid and distilled water, respectively. Furthermore, these fraction specifications are conretized by relational qualities (volume) proportion of nitric acid and (volume) proportion of distilled water.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
